<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luchino Visconti (lord of Milan)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1287–1349</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luchino Visconti was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from 1339 until his death in 1349, ruling jointly with his brother Giovanni, archbishop of Milan. He greatly enlarged Visconti power in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, acquiring cities including Asti, Parma and Alessandria in the 1340s. He governed with a firm hand, and was rumoured to have been poisoned by his wife.</p></div>
